+::a19b1 This answer hangs on the first entry of that list, and it is a contribution in its own right. ::a19b2 Because it refers to statement `a19`, its key is `a19b`, and its own statements are keyed `a19b1`, `a19b2`, and so on.
+
+::a19b3 What that arrangement buys you:
+
+- ::a19b4 An answer appears directly underneath the statement it refers to. ::a19b5 **A statement is therefore tied to its context twice — by its key and by the place where it is shown.** Whole levels of answers can be folded away when a page gets crowded.
+- ::a19b6 An answer is set apart from the surrounding contribution by colour and indentation, so it stays visible whose text you are reading.
+- ::a19b7 Any number of parties can take part, each with its own letter and its own colour.
+- ::a19b8 Contributions may be written in Markdown.
+
+::a19b9 Because the context travels with the statement, quoting somebody out of context does not work here. ::a19b10 The surrounding text is always one click away, and it stays there.
